From bb76905934925dc96cf4421d78dfe8579ed1177e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vortiago <atle@havso.net>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 13:41:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] perf(ggml-cpu): vectorise the f32 sigmoid
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add ggml_v_sigmoid, 1/(1+ggml_v_expf(-x)), next to ggml_v_silu for every
ISA that has it (AVX512, AVX2, SSE2, SVE, NEON, RVV), and a row kernel
ggml_vec_sigmoid_f32 in vec.cpp on the same ISA ladder as
ggml_vec_silu_f32. It replaces the scalar inline ggml_vec_sigmoid_f32 in
vec.h, which had no callers.

The F32 GGML_UNARY_OP_SIGMOID path now calls the row kernel. F16, BF16
and use_ref keep the scalar libm path, so test-backend-ops on a CPU-only
machine compares the SIMD path against the scalar one.

The result is not bit-exact with libm expf: ggml_v_expf has a maximum
error of about 1.45 ulp + 0.5. On the test-backend-ops SIGMOID cases the
max abs error is 1.2e-07 and the NMSE is below 4e-17.

Ported from ik_llama.cpp PR 2457 ("Simdify sigmoid evaluations"). The
scope is f32 only.

